{%- doc -%}
  Little Row: echoes `true` when a sold-out buy button should read "notify me" and open the back
  in stock modal instead (blocks/back-in-stock.liquid, or the Amp app's popup without that block).
  That needs the "Notify me on sold out variants" theme setting, a product page showing its own
  product (both belong to the page's product), and a selected variant that exists but is
  unavailable.

  @param {object} product_resource - The product the button belongs to.
  @param {object} variant - The variant the button would add.

  @example
  {%- capture notify_me -%}{% render 'util-notify-me', product_resource: product, variant: variant %}{%- endcapture -%}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  if settings.notify_me_when_sold_out and request.page_type == 'product' and product_resource.id == product.id
    if variant != blank and variant.available == false
      echo 'true'
    endif
  endif
-%}
